SUMMARY:Music & Movement
DESCRIPTION:Who’s it for? Wiggle worms\, birth to age five\, and their 
 favorite grownups \n\nWhat will you do? Some people learn better when they 
 are moving. If that sounds like your child\, this is the storytime for you! 
 Sing\, dance and MOVE in this fun\, active program that builds reading 
 skills. \n\nWhat is your child learning? Children who love books and 
 stories become better readers.  \n\nUnless posted\, this program is held 
 every week at this time. \n\nSupport for early literacy programs is 
 provided by a grant from First Things First\, which partners with families 
 and communities to give all Arizona children the opportunity to arrive at 
 kindergarten healthy and ready to succeed. Learn more at 
 FirstThingsFirst.org.\n\nDo you require an accommodation to participate in 
 a Phoenix Public Library program\, service\, or activity? Call 
 602-262-4636\, TTY 711\, or submit your request in person or through Ask Us 
 at least 14 business days before the event. \n\n¿Necesita alguna 
 adaptación para participar en algún programa\, servicio o actividad de 
 Phoenix Public Library? Llame al 602-262-4636\, a la línea TTY al 711 o 
 presente una solicitud en persona o por medio de Ask Us por lo menos 14 
 días hábiles antes del evento.
LOCATION:Meeting Room\, Acacia Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Matthew Dieckman":MAILTO:matthew.dieckman@phoenix.gov
CATEGORIES:Childrens' Programs, Storytimes
